{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dev ops ai tool risk layers dev ops ai tool risk layers","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers.md","fileName":"DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps AI Governance]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps AI Governance","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dev ops ai tool risk layers dev ops ai tool risk layers","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers.md","fileName":"DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers","heading":"DevOps AI Tool Risk Layers","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"DevOps AI tools can be classified by where they participate: the IDE, pull-request collaboration, delivery pipelines, cloud model infrastructure, and security or compliance systems. Placement matters because a suggestion in an editor has a different blast radius from model output that influences a release artifact.\n\nRisk grows with access, authority, and proximity to production. An organization should identify which tools require network access or secrets, which are advisory, and which can affect delivery. The layer model turns a vague inventory of “AI tools” into an architecture whose permissions, policy, cost, and failure consequences can be reviewed explicitly.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps AI Governance","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pd